{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game","id":908097,"title":"Words One Never Expects to come out of a Wolf Game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-05T21:12:53-07:00","id":908097,"title":"Words One Never Expects to come out of a Wolf Game.","content":"Everything below was uttered during the course of but one game. I leave it here at the fervent prompting of my Players as either a warning to others. Or an invitation. You choose which.<br /> <br /> The Alpha: &quot;Our ideal is to not turn people into a tree&quot;<br /> The Rahu after some consideration: &quot;Our idea is to turn no more than one person into a tree.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Hunter in Darkness: &quot;I got 14 successes on the stealth roll to drag a bag of rats around new york city without anyone noticing&quot;<br /> The Hunter in Darkness: &quot;Let's not plant the rat-tree in OUR backyard&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;Talk to the regular rats first, then talk to the rat-tree, then talk to the new rat&quot;<br /> The Bone Shadow in responce: &quot;No let's start with the theoretically hopeful rat.&quot;<br /> Alpha to the Rahu: &quot;If you two don't look into each each other's eyes, it doesn't count.&quot;<br /> Rahu to Mage &quot;Wait a minute, I've heard that before, what is he trying to hold?&quot;<br /> The insane Bone Shadow: &quot;Speak rat to me&quot;<br /> <br /> The sane Iron Master: &quot;Are we using the Mountain Dew to perform homeopathic medicine&quot; (Mountain Dew is a the term my players use for the Distilled Essence they are pumping up using fragments of God Machine Infrastructure&quot;<br /> The Rahu: &quot;My battle paddle is a fetish!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me; I am so ashamed: &quot;The rat lets out a long squeal of both pain, and disturbingly, pleasure.&quot;<br /> The Alpha: &quot;We just made a BDSM rat.<br /> The Hunter in Darkness: &quot;Sure guys, let's just talk to the BDSM rat, I'm sure it'll tell us something useful&quot;<br /> <br /> Te Hunter in Darkness: &quot;Did we just create rat Moses?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Player of the sane Iron Master: &quot;Do you have dots in language: Hobo Cant&quot;<br /> The Iron Master: &quot;Did you turn him into a hobo tree? Is henow going to plant his roots and spread the fruits of homelessness?&quot;<br /> Me again. Still ashamed: &quot;This dude has a lot of homelessness resonance.&quot;<br /> Still Me: &quot;Very lacking in monetary resonance.&quot;<br /> The Hunter: &quot;Will the fire touched eventually call us out for being inhumane?&quot;<br /> The Hunter Again: &quot;So your plan is uplift the spirit of new york city by feedin the poor poisonous hope?&quot;<br /> What I thought was my sane Iron Master: &quot;New Aspiration: Raise Hope Pigeon army to shit on Crow hosts.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;We are polluting with hope, we can't let this happen!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Rahu Blood Talon: soooo many of these quotes are mine...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:21:31-07:00","id":908103,"title":"","content":"What. Even. Happened.<br /> <br /> What am I looking at, beyond the sacred gifts of heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:29:39-07:00","id":908109,"title":"","content":"Ah, to game whilst under the influence. Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:30:33-07:00","id":908113,"title":"","content":"Introducing crossover to werewolf results in weird things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:43:13-07:00","id":908121,"title":"","content":"The possibly last game of a very long, fruitful, funny, heart warming and utterly terrifying Wolf game involving a Preppy rich boy werewolf, a near miss mage, a put upon former gang member, a time hopping werewolf and a former child solider all shoved into new york after it was spiritually nuked off the face of the earth 10 years prior by something no one knows about. Our job was to rebuild the city's territories and reclaim land before the pure did.<br /> <br /> It went weirdly.<br /> <br /> We might have to end it here, but if we don't we might go up against the very essence of the void or go after another pack stuck in the underworld, we also have to convince the now surrounded fire touched pack not to try a coup against the other forsaken, not end up being beaten to death by the spirit of the brooklyn bridge, and deal with a rogue court that is partly our fault because we decided the most innocent spirit we could use as a leader for it was a hotdog cart.<br /> <br /> We were terribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11725-spartacus_lance","user":"Spartacus_Lance","date":". 06-06-2016, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11725-spartacus_lance","name":"Spartacus_Lance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:45:32-07:00","id":908123,"title":"","content":"Also don't ask about Princeton. We don't talk about Princeton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11725-spartacus_lance","name":"Spartacus_Lance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:46:39-07:00","id":908124,"title":"","content":"Explanation: we stole an entire infrastructure, and were testing the effects of the essence it produced on various things (after accidentally turning the pack leader into a tree and also accidentally giving the Rahu mage sight attuned to time), we decided the &quot;stick your dick in it and hope for the best&quot; method of testing new things was a bad idea, so we fed some rats essence infused with totemic essence (our totem is a magath, combining hope, self-improvement, and plants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:43:13-07:00","id":908149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spartacus_Lance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game?p=908121#post908121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">time hopping werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>tindalos.wav","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T23:19:10-07:00","id":908171,"title":"","content":"Just let it be known. If you give a couple Wolves an Essence Distilling machine. Expect horrific miracles. The Alpha was cringing when the Bone Shadow 'Beast Talked' with the &quot;Lab&quot; rats.<br /> <br /> Lab rats who escaped, by the way; out into the middle of Manhattan. All ten of them are the size of Great Danes and somewhat self aware thanks to being infused with raw hope Essence. They may also suffer from the Opened Condition.<br /> <br /> Great Hunts lie ahead. Especially now that the resident Hatara Bastet and his Pride have been made aware. Lets hope the &quot;Good&quot; guys find the escapees before the mysteriously absent Beshilu do. In New York, Animals rule the streets. And they don't always howl. And now those streets are becoming crowded. The once spiritually dead City now has Hisil. And with Manhattan restored, so comes the Crown of Spirit of New York.<br /> <br /> This story is long, complex, and recorded on audio thanks to my foresight. So I can say with pride. This Story is True.<br /> For now It is enough to understand the Pack want this Crown on the head of their Totem. They believe they can rig the process by distilling the Essence of their Totem and Turf and dropping it into the water supply of the City. Thereby tainting/influencing the City into resonance with the Totem.<br /> <br /> Tonight was research on what was safe and what was not. Fortunately for the City. This Pack now knows how much is too much. Unfortunately ten rats larger than most dogs paid the price. (as well as one homeless dude who got a free drink out of the deal.<br /> I should also mention that this Pack may be a year old. But they have weathered the machinations of a rogue Arch-Master, faced off with a Host of Techno-Humonculi. Been constantly threatened and saved by a Guardian unwilling to do his fucking job. Beat the shit out of Hatara Bastet with Daddy issues, and currently hold the keys to one of(if not the) largest Low Place on the planet.<br /> The have spoken with Snake and smiled with Death on the shore of the Oroboros. They had two packmates trade places across ten years of time thanks to the Paradox of the Alpha's girlfriend. A Bound wants the Alpha dead, the Boneshadow is Schrodinger's Void, the Rahu is a hairs breath from being a Time Lord and the Hunter has his Tribal Totem's tooth. The Iron Master stands out in that he managed to single-handedly win the Transportation Court to their Pack's allegiance and manages to off balance this insanity so long as he isn't drunk.<br /> <br /> The Pack literally searched The Internet, freed a lost First Born caged inside 4chan, and faced off with a Slender Man while crossing Something Awful.<br /> <br /> They settle problems with human disruption by causing mass hysteria. The fed the Spirit of Columbia Univeristy to their Totem, and ground an Angel into the very Machine it was using to take advantage of Time's Square New Years Party. They are best buds with a Dwarf and Gnome who run their favorite Butcher shop. And these Summer Courtiers owe<i> them</i> favors.<br /> <br /> And yes. They set up the a Spirit born of a Hot Dog cart to take over the Court of Central Park. Said Spirit may now have grown bigger than the pack can handle without the packs even more unwieldy Totem pulling Rank. All of this and I swear we still have yet to jump a single shark. The dice rolls are there for posterity. I'm sure I'm forgetting a lot of what this Pack has been through. They deserve every ounce of glory too come. But not before finding out how difficult it is NOT to become the monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","user":"Khalvin8","date":". 06-06-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:15:26-07:00","id":908319,"title":"","content":"I have read all of this, and I comprehend it all in a very intellectual manner.<br /> <br /> The original question still stands, because even seeing how it makes sense, it doesn't make sense. It's sense only makes sense when you acknowledge that it doesn't make sense, like Wonderland.<br /> <br /> What the what even happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T08:28:25-07:00","id":908352,"title":"","content":"To be fair none of us are completely sure. This particular thread of the game is kind of a one shot c plot That morphed into the answer for one of the A plots, Our pack controls columbia, though controls is kinda a ... misnomer. We claim it, but due to having a massive burgeoning territory its more just putting out fires wherever they pop up. Combine that with the fact that the only person willing to take alphaship is a failed stormlord turned &quot;ghost wolf&quot; who's made a deal with a mythical first born, and fires tend to pop up like mad.<br /> <br /> So at some point Dusty, our time hopping rahu, who was a frat boy in the 90's as part of his former pack, went to reclaim the frat house. Turns out we had interacted with said frat house before, and we found out that the formerly rowdy but sweet frat boys had turned into super academic stepford smilers. We searched the campus and found out that &quot;gun detectors&quot; had been installed since the riots that happened during new years, which we had caused to stop a city nuking attempt from the God Machine. It involved Blood Talons, Stolen Fire trucks, and lots of Spiritually awakened drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> So my Alpha Lance Penn, the recovering Affluenza sufferer and failed storm lord, decides that this is not good, but being a very dim bulb and very aware of it , decides to ask Carl , our near miss mage turned Bone shadow occultist, what we are dealing with all the while trying not to let him death rage due to loss of knowladge from his experiment he was running in the frat house.<br /> <br /> We originally think they are misting our student population with &quot;stepford stuff&quot; that causes them to feel docile and productive. Our Former child soldier turned hunter in darkness, now know as Mark suggests we bash them apart. Carl wants to just take them elsewhere. Dusty just thinks the frat boys are creepy. It is agreed that staging another violent answer is not a smart idea, not after princeton. We then proceed to roll up in a van and take them apart. When confronted my Alpha pulls Social rank, lies or if that fails uses money, to quiet people.<br /> <br /> You will note our Beta, Andre, is not here. This is the main reason why we as a pack now have 20 pieces of infrastructure in the back of the van. Knowing this is connected to the thing that nearly killed us before we decide to bury them underground near our portal to the underworld to keep them safe.<br /> <br /> We then take them to the Mages of boston, who figure out it's more draining from people something they can't explain to us. It hurts to contemplate, so we just chalk it up as &quot;Mountain Dew&quot; and we realize that mountain dew is Essence Jelly. Carl literally licks it off his fingers and get's like nine points of essence.<br /> <br /> Now skip forward a few weeks, we have been doing other things and Carl, being a curious fellow, talks our beta, who just got his engineering degree, into opening up one of the &quot;Mountain dew Dispensers&quot; to see how it worked. Much later I walk in and find them covered in the goop and having figured out it condenses the resonance around them. They want to know more and Lacy, Lance's girlfriend who was patching him up from our latest foray into Princeton is asked to give an opinion on the uses's of the new form of mountain dew. She mage stares it too hard and leaks herself into. Cue Dusty, who is all about the mind altering chems to the point of it being a trigger for him, stuffing it in his mouth. He now can listen to radio and watch tv from alternate timelines, but has no control over which one.<br /> <br /> While this is happening lacy goes home because she needs to rest and tells her friend and mentor malcolm, the guardian, that he might want to go contain this shit. Malcolm loves us, to the point of not having killed our bone shadow when he accidentally branded himself with the rune for death but this is going too far. He comes in and takes the stuff, we agree to let him take it, but not before dusty realizes we are taking his new chems away. He gobbles some more and gets stuck in gaurou. Thankfully he has a gift that allows him not to death rage out of control, I have a gift that forces people out of death rage, and he has enough essence to kill a horse. I get curious and being the dim bulb I am get talked into taking a shot.<br /> <br /> My beta is less than impressed when I start growing bark like hair and get stuck in near man form. He leaves for work, and it is in this moment of unsupervised absence that the Alpha and the Rahu hatch a plan, aided none too subtly by Carl. We know that this stuff can give whatever resonance to people, and we want our spirit to be king of New York, so if we taint the resonance of New york that will make it easier.<br /> <br /> We then start our experiments on rats as we wait for Malcolm to come back, at the urging of the Alpha NOT to kidnap random people or hobos and only after trying it on a dead rat to make sure it doesn't like... become the t-virus.<br /> <br /> When the rats start using the word brethren though.... well the rest is history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11725-spartacus_lance","user":"Spartacus_Lance","date":". 06-06-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11725-spartacus_lance","name":"Spartacus_Lance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:32:19-07:00","id":908423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Misterscruffles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game?p=908124#post908124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explanation: we stole an entire infrastructure, and were testing the effects of the essence it produced on various things (after accidentally turning the pack leader into a tree and also accidentally giving the Rahu mage sight attuned to time), we decided the &quot;stick your dick in it and hope for the best&quot; method of testing new things was a bad idea, so we fed some rats essence infused with totemic essence (our totem is a magath, combining hope, self-improvement, and plants).</div> </div> </div> </div>But the &quot;Stick your dick in it and hope for the best&quot; method is the only truly effective one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:55:47-07:00","id":908580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spartacus_Lance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game?p=908352#post908352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair none of us are completely sure. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Note here that Mage Girlfriend Lacy rolled dice to Scrutinize and overflowed the Rolls per Mage Rules. Staining the Distilled Resonance with her Acanthus Nimbus and giving me a ST heart attack. Especially when the Frat Rahu decides to test if this new concotion makes a good moonshine. Let's just admit that it certainly has a kick.<br /> Cue Acanthus drunk Rahu. The Rahu fell to Kuruth when a bottle of the stuff broke during attempts to keep it away from him. (I admit to taking opportunities to capitalize on my Pack's Triggers. Bad St.) And since he chugged more of the stuff. I opted to let consequences rain. If you drink a ton of Time infused Resonance and you have a quasi-Spiritual Pattern. Don't be surprised if that Pattern gets locked out of Temporal relativity when it aligns with the resonance thanks to the Laws of Spiritual Consumption. You are what you drink.<br /> <br /> All I can say is that letting things happen usually encourages the bizarre and awesome. And for my group. I let a lot fly because my group wants the moment when it blows up into chaos and Rat Trees and Zombies and Sleeping Old Ones beneath the Epic Cenote built from Werewolf bones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:12:09-07:00","id":908612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game?p=908109#post908109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, to game whilst under the influence. Good times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I play the Rahu, Dusty 'The Fratwolf' McGruff. I must be the one to inform you... the only person drunk was the Beta. I want to preface the following with that Dusty was in Garou with 19 str, something like 28 health boxes, and 6/6 armor and 5 auto-soak from gifts. Thanks to Giant, he stands 11'1&quot; and 2200lbs in garou form (equivalent to a large polar bear).<br /> <br /> Now the IC answer to &quot;what even happened&quot;<br /> <br /> So we found out that Mountain Dew was like, mad poisonous bro. And it gave you so much essence you were gonna explode! Then we found some collectors for it at my old college where I experienced my first change, and found out it turned the whole frat lame, bro. Like, there was no violence, no beer, and no sports. So Mark stole a bunch like a boss, and we were tryin' to reverse them, and give people back there creativity or somethin'. I dunno, Carl Carl'd, and then Lacy came down stairs and passed out and the Mountain Dew turned blue. I call it Pepsi. So we found out it reacted to some stuff, and I had some in my hand so... you know, I ate some. Just to see what would happen, you know, Bro?<br /> <br /> And that's when things got mad weird, Bro! So I saw the cord of magic that Lacy laid down that drew me into the future. By the way dudes, the robots in the future suck, but otherwise, the future is pretty sweet! And I figured that you know, if I just broke it, it'd snap me back in time and stuff. But anyway, so I was lookin' at my new packmates as they walked downstairs and Bro, they were flippin' weird. Like, this one guy had some sort of dagger in him, and another was loaded with scars on like, his soul. Or something. I dunno. Anyway right, so they take me upstairs and I see Lacy and I really just wanted some more Pepsi, right? But then I see the news and we start listening to the radio and I'm like 'man I can see the future, bro!' and then I realize it's not just the future, but like, alternate time lines!<br /> <br /> So Malcolm comes over, and he's a douche, but he's like, got a little blue in him too. And I really wanted some more of that blue, but I was chill, until Carl and Mark gave him ALL OF IT. Talk about buzzkill right? So when DoucheMage dropped one of the bottles, I totally snapped and uh... well I death raged out. And I just jumped on the puddle and was licking that stuff up, like, broken glass and all, right? And Lance jumps on me and stops the death rage and I pass out... then I woke up, and I was still in the Father's Form, bro! And I could feel the death rage, but it was like, off to the side.<br /> <br /> So I'm thinkin this DoucheMage looks like a good snack for some more blue, but he's gone. So they take me back downstairs, and they convince me to make this machine do something else, and Carl Carl's, and we get yellow, I think we're gonna call it Surge. And we're pretty sure it's like... hope and shit. So I convinced Lance to take a shot, and then I took a few shots of it, and he went all Dalu, and I was still in Garou, and our hair turned into thorns bro! But I was still pretty into the blue stuff and stuff.<br /> <br /> Anyway, fast forward, we catch a metric butt ton of rats, Malcolm drains all mine and pansy Lance's essence so I have to drop out of Garou, but I totally convinced him to turn my Battle Paddle into a Fetish! And I'm thinkin', we can totally dump these things in Leo's (or whatever cat dude's name is) apartment. I'm allergic to cats, but I figure he's huntin' Beshilu right now, what better prank than to drop a hundred or three mice into his place? And he's a cat dude, so he will be cool, right?<br /> <br /> Well then Carl and Mark start talkin' about experimentin' on the rats, and we figure out that we can make New York totally more 'Murica if we just give everyone some more hope, like in Ghostbusters, right Bro? We're gonna dump it into the city water supply. We just gotta figure out the how fast to dump it in, and how much we need. So we're figure out roughly the dose we want with the rats, and Carl thinks we turned one of the rats a little smarter or something, but whatever. They're in cases and stuff. So we go out and give a hobo a beer laced with this stuff, and he immediately starts feelin' like he can turn his life around accordin' to Andre.<br /> <br /> So we head back to the house and uh... there was giant rats bro. Like, big dog sized. Almost as big as my wolf form, right? Crazy. And they all ran off. So I figure, I can't go dumpin' rats on CatDouche now, so I just dump the problem on him instead. He's huntin' rats anyway, right bro?<br /> <br /> I'm totally still going to have Mark collect up another sack of rats and dump them in CatDouche's house while me and him go huntin' sometime. Just wait. Totally doin' it, Bro. Also, we're planting the rat tree's in his planter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:24:26-07:00","id":909362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908097-words-one-never-expects-to-come-out-of-a-wolf-game?p=908319#post908319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read all of this, and I comprehend it all in a very intellectual manner.<br /> <br /> The original question still stands, because even seeing how it makes sense, it doesn't make sense. It's sense only makes sense when you acknowledge that it doesn't make sense, like Wonderland.<br /> <br /> What the what even happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, combining Werewolf with other gamelines whose stuff Werewolf powers were never meant to handle results in a need for... creativity.<br /> <br /> Madness lies ahead.<br /> <br /> (This is also what happens when the player playing the one sane and reasonable character suddenly has his schedule tighten up and starts missing session time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}